IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mhw-dates`
IMPORT `mhw-rules`
IMPORT `mhw-seat`

-- Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) -- worked cases for the questions of the person the Act is applied to
-- (mhw-seat.l4), the date helpers (mhw-dates.l4) and the shared rules (mhw-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by
-- hand from the deposited text and a calendar; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim
-- about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
--
-- The calendar used: Monday 2 November 2026; Friday 6, 13, 20, 27 November and 4, 11, 18, 25 December 2026; Monday 30
-- November, 7, 14, 21, 28 December 2026; Friday 1 January 2027. Melbourne Cup Day is Tuesday 3 November 2026; Christmas
-- Day is Friday 25 December 2026; Boxing Day (Saturday 26 December 2026) is observed on Monday 28 December 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Dates`

-- Weekends: 7 and 8 November 2026 are a Saturday and a Sunday; 6 and 9 November a Friday and a Monday.
#ASSERT (`d` 7 11 2026) `falls on a weekend`
#ASSERT (`d` 8 11 2026) `falls on a weekend`
#ASSERT NOT ((`d` 6 11 2026) `falls on a weekend`)
#ASSERT NOT ((`d` 9 11 2026) `falls on a weekend`)
-- 10 business days after Friday 6 November 2026: 9-13 and 16-20 November, so Friday 20 November; with one holiday,
-- Monday 23 November. 20 after it: Friday 4 December. 2 before Wednesday 11 November: Monday 9 November.
#ASSERT `the last of` 10 `business days after` (`d` 6 11 2026) `with` 0 EQUALS `d` 20 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 10 `business days after` (`d` 6 11 2026) `with` 1 EQUALS `d` 23 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 20 `business days after` (`d` 6 11 2026) `with` 0 EQUALS `d` 4 12 2026
#ASSERT `the latest day` 2 `business days before` (`d` 11 11 2026) `with` 0 EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
-- Weekdays after Friday 13 November up to Friday 27 November: 10. After Monday 16 November: 9.
#ASSERT `the weekdays after` (`d` 13 11 2026) `up to` (`d` 27 11 2026) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the weekdays after` (`d` 16 11 2026) `up to` (`d` 27 11 2026) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the weekdays after` (`d` 27 11 2026) `up to` (`d` 13 11 2026) EQUALS 0
-- 6 months after 31 August 2026 is 28 February 2027 (no 31st); 12 months after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029

§§ `Shared rules`

-- s 3: a patient, an eligible patient, a young patient.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- a patient` `an assessment order`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 -- a patient` `no order`)
#ASSERT `s 3 -- an eligible patient` `a forensic patient order`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 -- an eligible patient` `an assessment order`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 -- an eligible patient` `a court assessment order`)
#ASSERT `s 3 -- a young patient` `a treatment order` 17
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 -- a young patient` `a treatment order` 18)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 -- a young patient` `no order` 15)
-- ss 142, 143: all four limbs.
#ASSERT `s 142 -- the compulsory assessment criteria apply` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 142 -- the compulsory assessment criteria apply` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 143 -- the compulsory treatment criteria apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- The duty helper at the deadline (day 27), the day after, and still open.
#ASSERT `what became of` (`s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` 27) `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` TRUE `at` 27 `now` 27 EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `what became of` (`s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` 27) `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` TRUE `at` 28 `now` 28 EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `what became of` (`s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` 27) `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` FALSE `at` 0 `now` 27 EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `what became of` (`s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` 27) `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` FALSE `at` 0 `now` 28 EQUALS `not done in time`

§§ `Mental illness (s 4)`

#ASSERT `Would I be considered to have mental illness` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would I be considered to have mental illness` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only an s 4(2) matter (for example drug use itself): no.
#ASSERT `Would I be considered to have mental illness` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(3): the serious effects of drugs may indicate mental illness, if s 4(1) is met.
#ASSERT `Would I be considered to have mental illness` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would I be considered to have mental illness` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Assessment orders`

-- s 144(1)(a): examined 24 hours before is within "the previous 24 hours"; 25 is not.
#ASSERT `Can an assessment order be made on me` 24 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a community or an inpatient assessment order may be made`
#ASSERT `Can an assessment order be made on me` 25 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no assessment order may be made`
#ASSERT `Can an assessment order be made on me` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a community assessment order may be made, but not an inpatient one`
#ASSERT `Can an assessment order be made on me` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no assessment order may be made`
#ASSERT `Can an assessment order be made on me` 2 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no assessment order may be made`

-- s 147: community 24; inpatient received at hour 10: 34; received at hour 60: 72 (the earlier); not received: 72.
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` FALSE FALSE 0 `not varied` 0 0 0 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 10 `not varied` 0 0 0 EQUALS 34
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 60 `not varied` 0 0 0 EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE FALSE 0 `not varied` 0 0 0 EQUALS 72
-- s 165: received at hour 50 (72), extended twice by 24: 120. An extension of 30 counts as 24: received at 5, 29 + 24 = 53.
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 50 `not varied` 0 24 24 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 5 `not varied` 0 30 0 EQUALS 53
-- s 154(1): inpatient varied to community at hour 20, received at 5: earlier of 29 and 44 is 29; not received: 44;
-- received at 5 after a variation at 3: 27. s 154(2): community varied to inpatient at hour 10: 34.
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 5 `varied from inpatient to community` 20 0 0 EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE FALSE 0 `varied from inpatient to community` 20 0 0 EQUALS 44
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` TRUE TRUE 5 `varied from inpatient to community` 3 0 0 EQUALS 27
#ASSERT `When does my assessment order expire` FALSE TRUE 15 `varied from community to inpatient` 10 0 0 EQUALS 34

-- s 165: twice at most, and only if unable to decide.
#ASSERT `Can my assessment order be extended again` 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my assessment order be extended again` 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my assessment order be extended again` 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my assessment order be extended again` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ss 160, 175.
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated while on an assessment order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

